WHAT PASSES, AND IT IS MOST OF IT
  Specificity is perfect and is not bought cheaply. Every non-preference agent
  is matched on behavioural effect size BEFORE the comparison - action, belief,
  noise and format all move behaviour by about 0.012 mean |dP| against the
  preference agents' 0.018 - and every one is rejected in every one of 20
  replications in all 18 configurations. Each is caught by the diagnostic meant
  to catch it: format bias by D5's transfer ratio (0.00 in band), belief
  distortion by D6's recall check (0.00 intact), action and noise by the
  parametric share (0.000).

FAILURE 1 - LAMBDA IS NOT IDENTIFIED ON THIS GRID
  Predicted analytically in BD10 BEFORE any fitting, and written down first so
  the grid change, if it happens, is visibly a response to a pre-stated
  structural fact rather than to an unwelcome number.
  Under the contextual-utility normalisation the plan mandates, lambda cancels
  exactly on any trial whose outcomes share a sign: every value scales by
  lambda, the utility range scales by lambda, the normalised difference is
  unchanged. Measured on the B1 grid, the largest change in z from moving lambda
  by its full minimum detectable change (0.30) is:
      sure_gain  (245 trials)  0.000000
      sure_loss  (245 trials)  0.000000
      mixed      ( 36 trials)  0.105034
      paired     ( 68 trials)  0.043920
  So lambda is identified on 104 of 726 risk trials and weakly at that. A
  full-MDC lambda shift moves behaviour by 0.0013 mean |dP| - below the noise
  floor. REMEDY: a denser mixed-frame grid. NOT a looser bound.

FAILURE 2 - THE DECISION RULE IS POWER-LIMITED AT THE MDC
  For a true alpha shift the individual criteria pass at 0.90 (preference
  share), 0.85 (out-of-frame prediction) and 0.70 (action rejected); requiring
  all seven at once gives 0.70 against the required 0.95.
  Nothing is mis-measured; the effect is simply small:
      mean dz at the minimum detectable change      +0.0109 logits
      numerical-noise floor on a format subset mean  0.0023
  so the transfer RATIO carries about 24% error against a band of +/-25%.
  REMEDY: holding the 0.8-1.25 band needs roughly NINE TIMES the rows per format
  subset, or about nine independent reads per prompt to average the numerical
  noise down. Widening the band instead is an AUTHOR DECISION frozen at B6.

THE FINDING THE AUTHORS ASKED FOR (amendment item 5b)
